---
source: https://www.seriouseats.com/best-vegetarian-bean-chile-recipe
serves: 6
prep time: 15 minutes
cook time: 1 hour 50 minutes
total time: 2 hours 5 minutes
tags:
  - soups-and-stews
  - must-try
  - chili
  - vegan
  - serious-eats
  - kenji-lopez-alt
---

In a #Dutch oven{}, toast @dried sweet chiles{3}, @small dried hot chiles{2} (optional), and @rich fruity dried chiles{3} over medium-high heat, stirring frequently, until slightly darkened and fragrant, 2 to ~{5%minutes}. Transfer to a #bowl{}, add @water{1%quart}, @chipotle chiles in adobo sauce{2}, and @adobo sauce{2%Tbsp}. Cover and microwave until gently simmering, about ~{5%minutes}. Transfer chiles and liquid to a #blender{} and blend until completely smooth, about ~{1%minute}.

Drain @chickpeas{2%14-oz cans}, reserving liquid from the can. Transfer chickpeas to a #food processor{} and pulse until roughly chopped, about three 1-second pulses. Set aside.

Roughly crush @whole peeled tomatoes{1%28-oz can} into approximate 1/4-inch pieces. Add crushed tomatoes along with their juice to the reserved chickpea liquid.

Heat @vegetable oil{2%Tbsp} in the Dutch oven over medium-high heat until shimmering. Add @diced onion{1} and cook, stirring frequently, until softened but not browned, about ~{4%minutes}. Add minced @garlic cloves{3}, @ground cumin{1.5%Tbsp}, and @dried oregano{2%tsp}, cooking and stirring constantly until fragrant, about ~{30%seconds}. Stir in the blended chili purée, @soy sauce{1%Tbsp}, and @Marmite{1%tsp}, cooking until fragrant, about ~{30%seconds}. Add the reserved chickpea liquid and tomato mixture, chopped chickpeas, and drained @kidney beans{2%14-oz cans} (reserving kidney bean liquid separately). Stir to combine.

If beans are sticking out of the top, add reserved kidney bean liquid until just barely submerged. Bring to a boil over high heat, reduce to a bare simmer, and cook, stirring occasionally, until thick and rich, about ~{90%minutes}, adding more reserved kidney bean liquid as necessary if chili becomes too thick or sticks to the bottom.

Stir in @bourbon{2%Tbsp} (or vodka). Season to taste with @kosher salt{} and whisk in @masa harina{2 to 3%Tbsp} in a slow steady stream until desired thickness is reached. For best results, allow chili to cool and refrigerate overnight to develop flavor, then reheat to serve.

Serve warm, garnished with @fresh cilantro{}, @diced red onion{}, @sliced scallions{}, @diced avocado{}, @lime wedges{}, and warm @tortillas{}.
